From: Simon McVittie <smcv@debian.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Sep 2024 11:36:29 +0100
Subject: render: Make fix-shaders.sh work with GNU sed

Tested on Debian testing/unstable with GNU sed 4.9.

Resolves: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/issues/10878
Signed-off-by: Simon McVittie <smcv@debian.org>
Forwarded: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/10879
---
 src/render/gpu/shaders/fix-shaders.sh | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/render/gpu/shaders/fix-shaders.sh b/src/render/gpu/shaders/fix-shaders.sh
index 61d8138..f80adb2 100755
--- a/src/render/gpu/shaders/fix-shaders.sh
+++ b/src/render/gpu/shaders/fix-shaders.sh
@@ -2,5 +2,5 @@
 #
 # Update generated shader code to fix compiler warnings
 
-sed -i '' 's,^const,static const,' *.h
-sed -i '' 's,const unsigned,const signed,' *.dxbc.h
+sed -i -e 's,^const,static const,' *.h
+sed -i -e 's,const unsigned,const signed,' *.dxbc.h
